import opaquemod.{Asy}

-- ⚠️ WHAT THIS GATE CAN AND CANNOT SEE.  `diff_compiler_check_modules.sh` diffs the
-- entry's inferred SCHEMES against `oracle.tcmod`; it discards stderr and never reads
-- the exit code.  So this fixture guards the SILENT halves of #804/#1028 — a scheme
-- that comes back with the effect row erased — and it CANNOT guard the rejection half.
-- `speak` below is the #804 interface shape, and its printed scheme is BYTE-IDENTICAL
-- before and after the fix: the spurious `T-EFFECT-UNDETERMINED` went to stderr, which
-- this gate throws away.  The accept assertion for that shape lives in
-- test/analyze_project_fixtures/804_opaque_row_iface_accept/ (zero diagnostics, via
-- `check --json`), and `speak` is kept here because `runIt` at the bottom needs it.
export interface Speak s where
  speak : s -> Asy e a -> <e> a

-- #1028: a WRITTEN row in the Row-kinded slot must elaborate AS A ROW.  Without the
-- imported param kinds `fromAstTypeApp` fell through to `appFallback` instead of
-- `foldAppKinds`/`kindArgMono`.  Through THIS probe that failed SILENTLY — the golden
-- below read `Asy Unit Int` with nothing on stderr at all.  (On the `check`/`run`/`build`
-- CLI paths the same line instead drew a false-positive T-EFFECT-KIND-MISMATCH claiming the
-- slot "isn't row-kinded"; that is the loud face of this identical defect.)
wrote : Asy <Stdout> Int
wrote = wrote

-- The same row in its pre-#997 parenthesized spelling.  This one failed
-- SILENTLY: it typechecked with the row erased to the wrapped type, so the
-- golden below would read `Asy Unit Int` — indistinguishable, to the reader of a
-- scheme dump, from a genuinely dropped effect.
seeded : Asy (<Stdout> Unit) Int
seeded = seeded

-- The same bug's FOURTH face, NOT a control — do not delete this as redundant.
-- A bare tyvar in the row slot propagates cross-module for a `public export` type
-- (that is `effect_var_row_ctor_import`'s ground), but for an OPAQUE one it did not:
-- on a pre-fix binary this inferred `Speak a => a -> Asy b c -> c`, the row slot read
-- as an ordinary type parameter — the LAUNDERING answer, and silent. Post-fix it is
-- `Asy <> b -> b`, with the slot recognised as a row. So this line is a fourth
-- discriminator on the same root cause, and the golden below records the difference.
runIt : Speak s => s -> Asy b c -> c
runIt s a = speak s a
